      "text": "To determine the length of the tunnel, we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the speed of the train:**\n   The train is moving at a speed of 60 miles per hour.\n\n2. **Determine the time it takes for the train to exit the tunnel:**\n   The train takes 3 minutes to completely exit the tunnel. Since there is no mention of any additional time for the train to slow down or stop once it leaves the tunnel, we will use the given time directly.\n\n3. **Convert the time from minutes to hours:**\n   Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, 3 minutes is equivalent to:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{60} = \\frac{1}{20} \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total distance traveled by the train in the given time:**\n   The train travels at a speed of 60 miles per hour, and it takes \\(\\frac{1}{20}\\) hours to travel out of the tunnel. Therefore, the total distance traveled by the train is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 60 \\text{ miles per hour} \\times \\frac{1}{20} \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Relate the distance traveled to the length of the train and the tunnel:**\n   The total distance traveled by the train is the sum of the length of the train and the length of the tunnel. Let \\( L \\) be the length of the tunnel. The length of the train is 1 mile. Therefore, we have:\n   \\[\n   1 + L = 3\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for the length of the tunnel:**\n   \\[\n   L = 3 - 1 = 2\n   \\]\n\nThus, the length of the tunnel is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) miles.",
